## ❓ Essential Interview Questions

Q1: What is the exact file path of the main Active Directory database?
A1: C:\Windows\NTDS\ntds.dit

Q2: What is stored in the SYSVOL shared folder?
A2: C:\Windows\SYSVOL stores Group Policy Objects (GPOs) and logon/logoff scripts that replicate across all Domain Controllers.

Q3: Why are DNS SRV records vital for Active Directory?
A3: SRV records allow client computers to locate the specific servers providing domain services, such as Kerberos (Port 88) and LDAP (Port 389).